error: output port `o` is driven in more than one clock phase (on both sides of a `clk.tick().await`) in a shape whose synthesized form shows one of the writes a cycle after the simulator does. A write with no input read before it in its own phase runs at its cycle's opening; once an input read precedes some write of `o` (its own operand, a branch condition, a wait loop's exit test), or on the linear multi-tick path, the port is emitted as an edge-sampled register and that write lands one observation late (measured, phase E). Accepted shapes: no write of `o` preceded by an input read in its phase (a read in another phase is fine), or every write of it following an input read with a `clk.tick().await` after it (all writes then land at the edge on both sides). Otherwise declare `o` as `RegOut<…>` (a registered output, immune because it commits at the clock edge), or drive it in exactly one phase. If this module exists to DEMONSTRATE the divergence, opt out explicitly with `#[hardware(sequential, allow_pretick_alignment)]`.
